            <ArticleTitle>Left main coronary artery embolism: a case report.</ArticleTitle>
            <Pagination>
                <MedlinePgn>394-7</MedlinePgn>
            </Pagination>
            <Abstract>
                <AbstractText>A 27-year-old man had recurrent myocardial infarction found to be due to coronary embolism to the left main coronary artery with downstream embolization. The presumed etiology of thromboembolism was idiopathic cardiomyopathy. A unique method of treatment with Fogarty catheter retrieval was used.</AbstractText>
            </Abstract>
